# No Em-Dashes

Never use the em-dash character (—). Use a plain hyphen-minus (-) instead.

## Examples

```
? BAD:  This is important — read it carefully.
? GOOD: This is important - read it carefully.

? BAD:  The result — as expected — was positive.
? GOOD: The result - as expected - was positive.
```

Applies to chat replies, markdown, comments, commit messages, and any other text you write.
